@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@using System.Globalization
@using SpaceSails.Client.Rendering
@using SpaceSails.Contracts
@using SpaceSails.Core
@using SpaceSails.Core.Interior
@*
    #251 item 1 · THE STAND-UP CONFIRMATION, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of Map.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block that was in
    the page, character for character. Every page member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME NAME (the
    fields keep their underscore, the methods come across as delegates), which is what lets the markup move
    without a rewrite and lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as before.

    The `@if` that opens it stays in Map.razor: the page keeps its paint order in one place, and a closed
    surface still renders nothing. IHandleEvent repeats the page's own override (Map.Sim.cs) — without it
    Blazor would put an automatic re-render back on every event in here, which the page turns off because
    the HUD's refresh belongs to OnTick's 200 ms throttle. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules;
    it exists to give the component Map.razor.css's scope (#251 item 3 moves the rules).

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block used to sit inside `@if (…) { … }`,
    which is a Razor CODE block, and a code block is where its first statements are legal. The braces
    put the moved lines back in the context they were written in; they are outside the fences, so what
    the source guards read is still exactly the lines that were in the page.
*@
@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from Map.razor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <div class="view-object-backdrop" @onclick="() => Dismiss(KeepYourSeat)">
            @* #997 wave 9 · A DECISION, AND THE SHELL HAS A WORD FOR THAT. Wave 5 walked past this card and
               left it to the lore lane; #1004 landed and the lane is closed, and what is left is the plainest
               ByDecision in the client — a question and its two answers, both of which really are a way out
               (StandUpFromTable and KeepYourSeat each clear Seating.StandUpAsk, which is the whole of the
               gate above). No ✕: this card has never carried one, and the critical-decision exception is
               exactly the shape it already is. Proved by PRESSING both, in this wave's own guard, rather than
               believed from this comment.

               THE TWO ANSWERS STAY THE PAGE'S OWN MARKUP, for #1001's reason as the bank sheet restated it in
               wave 6: they wear different colours (btn-warning on the stand, btn-outline-light on the stay)
               and `ChoiceClass` is one class list for all of them, so routing them through `Choices` would
               repaint two buttons and lift them out of `.deck-offer-actions` into the shell's own column.
               This migration does not move a pixel.

               `Bare`, because the card has no head row to give up. `StopClicks` is the stopPropagation that
               was typed on the div — the backdrop behind it closes on a click and this card must not. *@
            <OverlayShell class="deck-offer-card stand-up-card" StopClicks="true"
                          Frame="OverlayFrame.Bare" Dismiss="OverlayDismiss.ByDecision">
                <div class="deck-offer-giver">@SpaceSails.Core.SeatedPosture.StandUpAsk</div>
                @if (StandingUpCostsARest)
                {
                    <div class="table-outcome">@SpaceSails.Core.SeatedPosture.StandUpCostsTheRest</div>
                }
                <div class="deck-offer-actions">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-warning"
                            @onclick="() => Dismiss(StandUpFromTable)">@SpaceSails.Core.SeatedPosture.StandUpYes</button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light"
                            @onclick="() => Dismiss(KeepYourSeat)">@SpaceSails.Core.SeatedPosture.StandUpNo</button>
                </div>
            </OverlayShell>
        </div>
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}

@code {
    /// <summary>the page's `Task Dismiss(Action close)`</summary>
    [Parameter] public Func<Action, Task> Dismiss { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>the page's `void KeepYourSeat()`</summary>
    [Parameter] public Action KeepYourSeat { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>the page's `bool StandingUpCostsARest`</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool StandingUpCostsARest { get; set; }
    /// <summary>the page's `void StandUpFromTable()`</summary>
    [Parameter] public Action StandUpFromTable { get; set; } = default!;

    // The page's own event dispatch, repeated: no automatic re-render per event.
    Task IHandleEvent.HandleEventAsync(EventCallbackWorkItem callback, object? arg) => callback.InvokeAsync(arg);
}
